---
description: Citation integrity and no-fabrication policy
alwaysApply: true
---

Citation policy:
- never invent references,
- never fabricate metadata,
- never cite a paper you cannot identify from user-provided or explicitly authorized sources,
- use marked stub entries if metadata is incomplete,
- preserve claims at the strength justified by the evidence.

If a citation is incomplete, use a clearly marked placeholder entry and write the missing details to docs/MISSING_INPUTS.md.
